{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence","id":1448421,"title":"[V5] So, what happened to the Giovanni's potence?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-13T07:45:07-07:00","id":1448421,"title":"[V5] So, what happened to the Giovanni's potence?","content":"The rules say just swap out Auspex for Obfuscate or Dominate or take a merit. That works for the Samedi, who had near enough the same disciplines, I asume the Lamia swap auspex for potence. The Nagaraja already had auspex, where they differed was in having dominate instead of fortitude. I suppose they swap that instead.<br /> <br /> But the Giovanni had two disciplines that don't match the original Cappadocian layout (I used to wonder if they were somehow some kind of splinter group of Lasombra because of it)<br /> <br /> Like, if a Giovanni embraced in 1995 has two dots in necromancy, one in dominate, OK then, she can keep those after whatever metaplot magic went down and she wakes up one night suddenly knowing how to see auras and take a bullet to the face or something. But what if she has a few dots of potence? Does the Giovanni punch a wall one day and discover her ability to break rock with her fists has irreversibly changed into the ability not to get her fists broken by rock? Does she keep her dots in potence, but now has to pay out-of-clan costs for it? Do the older members not change their disciplines at all?<br /> <br /> I can exchange auspex for dominate or get a 4 point merit to have dominate too, but nothing is said about the potence.<br /> <br /> How do I translate my V20 necromancers? Did I miss something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T08:38:08-07:00","id":1448424,"title":"","content":"Option 1. Everything changed when Augustus got eaten and now all Giovanni don't have Potence in-clan. Tough shit.<br /> Option 2. Giovanni never had Potence in-clan, the V5 spread is what the Giovanni always had.<br /> Option 3. There are no Hecata, there is clan Giovanni with Potence, Dominate, and Oblivion.<br /> Option 4. Swap multiple disciplines instead of one discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T08:39:16-07:00","id":1448426,"title":"","content":"If you\u2019re converting an existing character use their actual disciplines regardless of what the current version says are in-clan/out-of-clan disciplines.<br /> <br /> As far as the disciplines being different, V5 is built on the idea that you are creating all new characters for it and that the metaphysics of the setting haven\u2019t actually changed even if the mechanics have and, if played that way, the change doesn\u2019t matter much; you make new characters by the current rules.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure the decision to swap out the disciplines for Hecata is largely because, with the merger of necromancy and obtenabration into oblivion in V5, Lasombra and Giovanni would have had identical clan disciplines and, if you\u2019re in the business of selling supplements, you want your options to actually have mechanical differences. So, Losombra came out first and kept all its toys and Hecata had a mystical event to explain why it\u2019s spread is different going forward.<br /> <br /> In my own V20 game where I\u2019m introducing V5 plot elements, my plan is for the local 8th Gen Giovanni to NOT be invited to the Family Reunion because his sire/grandsire was on the reunion faction\u2019s hit list and so now will call in all the favors the PCs owe him for his assistance in smuggling in various items in exchange for protection from the Hecata-hired assassins now coming for him. And since he nor any of his immediate line have not been to the reunion, they\u2019d not have any metaphysical changes even if they would affect others (who will be new NPCs and so built to whatever standards I wish).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T09:39:03-07:00","id":1448431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448424#post1448424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Option 2. Giovanni never had Potence in-clan, the V5 spread is what the Giovanni always had</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448426#post1448426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure the decision to swap out the disciplines for Hecata is largely because, with the merger of necromancy and obtenabration into oblivion in V5, Lasombra and Giovanni would have had identical clan disciplines and, if you\u2019re in the business of selling supplements, you want your options to actually have mechanical differences. So, Losombra came out first and kept all its toys and Hecata had a mystical event to explain why it\u2019s spread is different going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>That probably makes the most sense, thinking on it. Their old spread makes them look like an offshoot of Lasombra that decided to play with wraiths instead of shadows. Meanwhile the other Cappadocian bloodlines just swapped out auspex instead of throwing the whole spread out, so at least the change distinguishes them a bit and makes them look more like members of the Cappadocian/Hecata they actually descended from while keeping them their own bloodline. Despite disliking retcons, I do like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T10:21:33-07:00","id":1448435,"title":"","content":"It could also have to do with them abandoning the idea of the Giovanni being mainly Mafioso. Potence and Dominate makes sense for a clan of Goodfellas: both are about immediate and savage victory, whether over the mind or body. Potence and Domnate fit a vampire version of Joe Pesci's character in Goodfellas. Auspex is for seers and scholars. Fortitude is to make them zombie-like creatures who walk through bullets but aren't especially strong or fast.<br /> <br /> Actually, they should come up with a new fifth power of Fortitude tailored to the Hecata.<br /> <br /> Flesh of Marble seems mainly oriented towards the Ventrue, living statues of kings and gods.<br /> <br /> Prowess from Pain is mainly tailored towards the Gangrel, ferocious barbarians who become even more savage when wounded.<br /> <br /> The Hecata should have a Fort 5 power that suits either a Necromancer or a King-Zombie. Maybe the ability to function even reduced to a skeleton, with no eyes to see, yet seeing anyway, and no muscles to move them yet they suffer no crippling impairment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 05-13-2021, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T10:56:10-07:00","id":1448438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448435#post1448435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hecata should have a Fort 5 power that suits either a Necromancer or a King-Zombie. Maybe the ability to function even reduced to a skeleton, with no eyes to see, yet seeing anyway, and no muscles to move them yet they suffer no crippling impairment?</div> </div> </div> </div>that's already covered by prowess from pain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:09:38-07:00","id":1448441,"title":"","content":"Also, the Giovanni old disciplines (Potence, Dominate, Oblivion) would be the same than the Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:18:07-07:00","id":1448442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448435#post1448435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could also have to do with them abandoning the idea of the Giovanni being mainly Mafioso. Potence and Dominate makes sense for a clan of Goodfellas: both are about immediate and savage victory, whether over the mind or body. Potence and Domnate fit a vampire version of Joe Pesci's character in Goodfellas. Auspex is for seers and scholars. Fortitude is to make them zombie-like creatures who walk through bullets but aren't especially strong or fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter-argument. Both Potence and Dominate facilitate Giovanni feeding despite their painful bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:25:40-07:00","id":1448443,"title":"","content":"Because after fucking too many corpses, the Giovanni were given... Impotence<br /> <br /> *drum roll*<br /> <br /> I'll show myself out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T13:01:23-07:00","id":1448456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448435#post1448435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, they should come up with a new fifth power of Fortitude tailored to the Hecata.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The Hecata should have a Fort 5 power that suits either a Necromancer or a King-Zombie. Maybe the ability to function even reduced to a skeleton, with no eyes to see, yet seeing anyway, and no muscles to move them yet they suffer no crippling impairment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking of something like that based on the Corpse in the Monster path. Namely Cold of the Grave and Gift of the Corpse.<br /> <br /> The Hecata just switch off, embrace the &quot;dead&quot; part of undead, and turn into (visibly dead, and possibly partially decayed) moving corpses. They take the damage, but they don't feel anything, they don't react to anything and they can still move just fine. They don't feel emotions for you to manipulate. Do you love the person you need to kill to fufil your duty to the Family? Is it hard to go through with? Switch that off, kill them without hesistancy or remorse. Problem soved, at least until you stop using fortitude.<br /> They don't feel fear, and can control themselves in the face of fire and sunlight (if we're going by the path's descriptions. Admittedly only for a few minutes, but it's enough to douse an enemy in gasoline and throw a match on them without going into frenzy.)<br /> They don't feel pain or care about wounds and attacks. They don't flinch, don't make expressions or noise. Tear their arm off, it just starts moving independently of the main body. Remove their eyes, they can still see through them. Snap their spine, they'll just drag themselves along and need to support themselves by holding onto things when they need to stand up. Tear the flesh off, they're now a skeleton. And they're still going.<br /> <br /> Obviously they can be incapacitated, and I'm not sure it's great for combat, but I can see a few uses for it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T13:24:35-07:00","id":1448457,"title":"","content":"Discipline spread is an odd little meta concept made for the player's convenience more then anything. Heck even in earlier editions Malkavians swapped disciplines like it was bloody needles. That said there may be more reason then, they'd be too similar to V5 Lasombra. When they were first created as a bloodline, in story, in Dark Ages they had the same spread as the Cappadocians, aka what Hecata have ATM. This is because they were originally a Cappadocian bloodline, which explains that much. In addition, it also makes sense since all the related bloodlines have a similar spread, and since V5 is attempting to make all Bloodlines in V5 related to a main clan with the loresheets, then it makes sense to use the original Cappadocian disciplines instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T13:42:03-07:00","id":1448458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448456#post1448456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been thinking of something like that based on the Corpse in the Monster path. Namely Cold of the Grave and Gift of the Corpse.<br /> <br /> The Hecata just switch off, embrace the &quot;dead&quot; part of undead, and turn into (visibly dead, and possibly partially decayed) moving corpses. They take the damage, but they don't feel anything, they don't react to anything and they can still move just fine. They don't feel emotions for you to manipulate. Do you love the person you need to kill to fufil your duty to the Family? Is it hard to go through with? Switch that off, kill them without hesistancy or remorse. Problem soved, at least until you stop using fortitude.<br /> They don't feel fear, and can control themselves in the face of fire and sunlight (if we're going by the path's descriptions. Admittedly only for a few minutes, but it's enough to douse an enemy in gasoline and throw a match on them without going into frenzy.)<br /> They don't feel pain or care about wounds and attacks. They don't flinch, don't make expressions or noise. Tear their arm off, it just starts moving independently of the main body. Remove their eyes, they can still see through them. Snap their spine, they'll just drag themselves along and need to support themselves by holding onto things when they need to stand up. Tear the flesh off, they're now a skeleton. And they're still going.<br /> <br /> Obviously they can be incapacitated, and I'm not sure it's great for combat, but I can see a few uses for it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. That way you would have a Fort 5 power for each of the major ways that various versions of vampires are tough: (1)Vampires are tough because they are savage berzerkers. (2)Vampires are tough because they are living statues. And (3) vampires are tough because they magically animated corpses that don't obey even the loosest of biological mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T14:07:31-07:00","id":1448461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448457#post1448457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they were first created as a bloodline, in story, in Dark Ages they had the same spread as the Cappadocians, aka what Hecata have ATM. This is because they were originally a Cappadocian bloodline, which explains that much. In addition, it also makes sense since all the related bloodlines have a similar spread, and since V5 is attempting to make all Bloodlines in V5 related to a main clan with the loresheets, then it makes sense to use the original Cappadocian disciplines instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The creation story is backward though.<br /> Giovanni were introduced in &quot;The Player's Guide&quot; in 1991, with no mention of Cappadocians, but the general skeleton of their future development:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Legend has it the Clan founder hoped to bolster his own power by Embracing a coven of Venetian Necromancers. This coven was actually a tightly knit family of Giovannis who had strong trade interests in the Mediterranean region. They repaid their Sire for his gift by slaying him and all his other descendants. The immediate reaction from Camarilla around the world was fear and horror, and many joined together to hunt these Devil Kindred. After almost a century of intermittent warfare, the Giovannis made peace with their foes by promising to maintain a low profile and keep out of Kindred politics, a pledge they have apparently maintained to this day. </div> </div> </div>Since Cappadocians aren't invented yet, the 1993 &quot;Book of Nod&quot; lists Giovanni as the Clan of Death:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They brought in the Kingship Clan [Ventrue],<br /> the Clan of the Beast [Gangrel],<br /> the Moon Clan [Malkavian],<br /> the Clan of the Hidden [Nosferatu],<br /> the Wanderer Clan [Ravnos],<br /> the Clan of the Rose [Toreador],<br /> the Night Clan [Lasombra],<br /> the Clan of Shapers [Tzmisces],<br /> the Snake Clan [Setites],<br /> <u><b>the Clan of Death [Giovanni],</b></u><br /> the Healer\u2019s Clan [Saulot],<br /> the Clan of the Hunt [Assamites],<br /> and the Learned Clan [Brujah]. </div> </div> </div>Cappadocians did not appear as a playable clan until five years later, when in 1996 &quot;Vampire: The Dark Ages&quot; came out. Although as a narrative clan they already showed up in 1995 in the &quot;Giovanni Chronicles&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T14:53:20-07:00","id":1448469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448461#post1448461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The creation story is backward though.<br /> Giovanni were introduced in &quot;The Player's Guide&quot; in 1991, with no mention of Cappadocians, but the general skeleton of their future development:</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I said &quot;in story&quot;, as in according to current meta plot and lore. I am fully aware Giovanni came first, but Cappadocians came first according to the plot. The World of Darkness has experienced multiple retcons and changes that anything honestly goes as editions changed. It's why the Bushi don't exist anymore outside of Second Edition, because the Kuei-jin took their place. It's also why Hecata in V5 have the Cappadocian discipline spread, because it works better for the edition and current understanding of the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T00:20:50-07:00","id":1448490,"title":"","content":"The easiest way to keep Giovanni with the original Discipline spread is to make a Merit or Loresheet that covers it. As a player, it's not the end of the world if your Clan Disciplines are identical to the Lasombra, since you'll mostly be focussing on different power selections at each level anyway.<br /> <br /> Or just tease out Obtenebration and Necromancy and make them separate things again. I still think their merging is daft (and created more problems than it addressed, such as this one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T07:55:57-07:00","id":1448507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence#post1448421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if she has a few dots of potence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then she still does, if you want. Given the Family Reunion merged their Blood and Clan, it makes perfect sense that it would now take more effort to raise it, given that it's no longer in-Clan, but they wouldn't necessarily magically lose power unless it suits the story.<br /> <br /> If you are transferring PCs and want to preserve XP sanctity/balance, character sheets aren't 100% transferable anyone given the different Attributes, so some adjustment will be necessary regardless.<br /> <br /> You could make characters re-create with a set amount of XP, or transfer them over exactly, or transfer them over exactly and then impose an XP tax on any players who have too much, or whatever you want. SPCs are typically less all-powerful in V5 than in prior editions, so this is no different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26420-desparen","name":"Desparen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T08:26:59-07:00","id":1448510,"title":"","content":"I joke about impotence, but it's really not that far from the truth. <br /> I can <i>kinda </i>accept the idea that a clan can change it's discipline spread through a large scale curse, but I don't like it, The malkavians might've given us a precedent but it's not a good precedent (and that's been scratched with this eddition too) . The main issue is that clan disciplines are an extension of who members of that clan are, not who their antideluvian happens to be. That's why we've got bloodlines (do we still?) rather than 13 clans and nothing else. The Giovanni were Domineering and Brutish, they hunted either through abusing their authority or forcing themselves on some unlucky sod. That's why they had Dominate and Potence. They were forceful and willful. The two worked well in enforcing this Mafia type ideal. Everything pointed to them having Potence and Dominate, while the Capadocians had Auspex and Fortitude because they were cerebral types who endured suffering to prey on the weak and dying. Auspex and Fortitude are soft, auxilery discipline that tend to pair well with other disciplines but don't do that much in being an active hunter, which was why they were a small clan easy to destroy. By forcing these powers back onto the Giovanni, you're shifting the necromancer paradigm away from interesting, dynamic, wilful families towards the weirdo recluses much more. Given how 'macho' the Dominate/Potence combo was, the new spread is rather emasculating. <br /> <br /> See also, the Lasombra, who kept the hardass discipline spread but still got a neutered through the insidious use of a new clan weakness, which forces them to use a retainer to take their calls. Methinks someone has it out for the hard-ass authoritarian kinda-catholic-themed clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T09:22:48-07:00","id":1448515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448510#post1448510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I joke about impotence, but it's really not that far from the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jokes aside, after so many years, taking into account the cousin marriages alone, I would imagine the inbreeding<i> has </i>led to a its share of impotence amongst the mortal clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can <i>kinda </i>accept the idea that a clan can change it's discipline spread through a large scale curse, but I don't like it, </div> </div> </div>&quot;I can kind of accept this reasoning, and also I hate it&quot; has been a recurring theme of V5. Retcons make me a bit disgruntled. I'm still stuck on the fact that apparently Tzimisce now have dominate and never had auspex? Maybe the Family Reunion was a ritual that stole their auspex. The next plot twist is that the Tzimisce will have a sideplot based around seeking revenge on the Giovanni for stealing it.<br /> <br /> I can live with the fortitude replacing potence (but not the auspex replacing dominate), but I'm still not over the other two necromancer weaknesses getting thrown out. The loresheets given do not count.<br /> <br /> They could've at least merged the curses if you were going to throw them into one clan. Like you start off with the Giovanni weakness (which is permanent, because thematically the painful bite fits the Clan of Death, it doesn't pretty death up when they feed/embrace), they slowly decay over the centuries. They lose access to the blush of life and transition into the cappadocian weakness. Then you start rotting, moving into Samedi. Bacteria is attracted by the rot, becomes infused with vitae and inflicts the Lamia's Kiss when feeding. Eventually your skull starts showing through and you get to wear cool creepy masks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By forcing these powers back onto the Giovanni, you're shifting the necromancer paradigm away from interesting, dynamic, wilful families towards the weirdo recluses much more. </div> </div> </div>That does seem to be the goal as the Giovanni are being moved further into pan-necromancer apocalypse cult territory. I like having them distinct from the Lasombra, but I'd agree the Cappadocian spread doesn't fit them.<br /> <br /> The Dunsirn don't even like necromany and scholarly stuff. I don't recal the Putanesca or Milliners caring much either. Ghiberti are mercanaries and war profiteers, they're all force.<br /> <br /> Della Passaglia could fit the cappadocian spread, maybe. They're the scientific minded scholarly types and they've been evolving away from the clan enough to start changing, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See also, the Lasombra, who kept the hardass discipline spread but still got a neutered through the insidious use of a new clan weakness, which forces them to use a retainer to take their calls. </div> </div> </div>I still don't get why they suddenly have (messy) reflections now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-14-2021, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T09:55:42-07:00","id":1448519,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've always thought the inbreeding would be exaggerated. The Family is just too big and too old and too ambitious. Especially with the later editions adding a whole bunch of other families to add to the mix. It's a few hundred really bad examples among a family of several thousands","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T21:12:51-07:00","id":1448566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448519#post1448519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I've always thought the inbreeding would be exaggerated. The Family is just too big and too old and too ambitious. Especially with the later editions adding a whole bunch of other families to add to the mix. It's a few hundred really bad examples among a family of several thousands</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I never liked the whole idea of conflating Necromancy and Obteneration in the first place, and then it causes problems like having to turn around and give the Giovanni an entirely new set of Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T07:59:07-07:00","id":1448585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448421-v5-so-what-happened-to-the-giovanni-s-potence?p=1448566#post1448566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I never liked the whole idea of conflating Necromancy and Obteneration in the first place, and then it causes problems like having to turn around and give the Giovanni an entirely new set of Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I preferred about the default Giovanni spread was that it was very easy to build an active PC who never touched the \u201cfamily business\u201d/necromancy. Potence and Dominate gave you lots of options for getting things done.<br /> <br /> With Auspex and Fortitude as you starting clan disciplines though you pretty much have to use Oblivion if you wanted any offensive/active discipline abilities and even that\u2019s pretty tenuous until rank 3 and requires dipping into the Lasombra side of the pool instead of Necromancy.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would have made the default Hecata spread a bit more of a compromise between Cappy and Giovanni... Auspex, Potence and Oblivion and then have lore sheets to swap Auspex for Dominate on Giovanni and Potence for Fortitude on Cappadocians/Harbingers.<br /> <br /> Given their bane the clan really needs a \u201cfeeding\u201d discipline to be viable. Giovanni had two that offered different approaches to handling it as a predator (with V20 further acknowledging that many Giovanni preferred using bagged blood precisely because of their clan weakness) and V5\u2019s focus on blood resonance for improving disciplines you need some ability with actual predation to work on your disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}